{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nI have just left the van Ghert house, where I sat at table with six children—five boys, one girl. The eldest, seventeen, is to come to Berlin in four years to complete his studies. They sent their warmest regards to you; I promised them the door would be open. A fine, bustling family. The wine was passable, though the roast beef was a trifle dry. I paid the usual modest sum for the evening’s hospitality.\n\nI walked back through the dark streets, thinking how strange it is to be a guest in another’s domestic sphere, observing the quiet machinery of a household while the world turns outside. It reminds one that the state is not merely an abstraction but a web of such particular lives.\n\nI am tired but content. The air here is cool. Do tell Karl I saw a boy who might do well with his geometry.\n\nYour affectionate\nG.W.F. Hegel"}}],"created":1795219160,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":197,"prompt_tokens":1114,"total_tokens":1311,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-hiwpBKE3mGWuV7nLVRRzVbY6XMsmi0H4","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":1114,"prompt_ms":1147.478,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.0300520646319569,"prompt_per_second":970.8247129792466,"predicted_n":197,"predicted_ms":4633.175,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.638647959183675,"predicted_per_second":42.303603900133275}}